**Problem:** We attempt to fill the composer without verifying the page is in a valid input state. This leads to fill timeouts when ChatGPT is showing modals, rate limits, or other blockers.

**Solution:** Add a pre-flight check before sendPromptAndWait.

```javascript
async function assertReadyForInput(page) {
  // Verify composer is visible and enabled
  const composer = page.locator(SELECTORS.composer).first();
  await composer.waitFor({ state: 'visible', timeout: 5000 });

  // Check no blocking modals
  const blockers = [
    '[data-testid="modal"]',
    '[role="dialog"]',
    'button:has-text("Upgrade")',
    // Add more as discovered
  ];
  for (const sel of blockers) {
    if (await page.locator(sel).isVisible({ timeout: 100 }).catch(() => false)) {
      throw new Error(`Page blocked by: ${sel}`);
    }
  }
}
```

**Location:** Call at start of sendPromptAndWait() in src/chatgpt.js, or in processRequest() in src/server.js.

**Benefit:** Fail fast with clear error instead of 30s timeout on fill.

