**Problem:** Even after fixing Undici timeouts, some stacks (proxies, VPN, etc.) can kill silent connections.

**Solution:** Send HTTP headers immediately + periodic whitespace to keep connection alive.

**Implementation:**
```javascript
async function handleRequest(req, res) {
  // Send headers immediately
  res.writeHead(200, {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json; charset=utf-8',
    // no Content-Length => chunked encoding
  });
  res.flushHeaders?.();

  // Heartbeat every 15s
  const heartbeat = setInterval(() => {
    res.write(' '); // whitespace keeps socket active
  }, 15_000);

  try {
    const response = await doLongRunningWork();
    clearInterval(heartbeat);
    res.end(JSON.stringify({ ok: true, text: response }));
  } catch (e) {
    clearInterval(heartbeat);
    res.end(JSON.stringify({ ok: false, error: String(e) }));
  }
}
```

**Note:** JSON allows leading whitespace, so response still parses correctly.

**Files:** src/server.js handleRequest()

